{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bqhtqkjlqdlbxdspeb4vfng7hxvrd2gkytyydgj66nmi5v4bhx6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe C library turned out to be small but I enumerated it properly first rather than assuming: `c_src/` is 4 files (`CMakeLists.txt`, `include/lib.h`, `src/lib.c`, `license.txt`) — a trimmed slice of Randy Gaul's `cute_c2`. I built it with CMake and ran `nm -D`, which gave **12 exported symbols**. No namespace-renaming macros were present (the header declares only `circle_collide`; the other 11 are non-`static` functions in `lib.c` that leak into the dynamic symbol table).\n\n## Completion gate — symbol diff is empty\n\n```\nC=12  RUST=12    missing from Rust: (none)    extras: (none)\nc2V  c2Mulvs  c2Maxv  c2Minv  c2Clampv  c2Sub  c2Dot\nc2CircletoCircle  c2CircletoAABB  c2CircletoCapsule\nc2Collided  circle_collide\n```\n\n## Differential verification\n\nRather than trust the build, I wrote a `dlopen` harness calling **all 12 symbols** in both `.so`s with identical inputs and comparing raw result **bytes** (so NaN payloads and `-0.0` vs `+0.0` are caught), across a 33-value edge-case table (±0, ±inf, ±NaN, denormals, `16777217`), a dense `circle_collide` grid, degenerate capsules, out-of-range `c2Collided` type tags, and 400k pseudo-random bit patterns:\n\n```\nchecks=3032134 fails=0\n```\n\n## The one real finding\n\nThe first run showed **192 mismatches**, all NaN sign-bit flips in `c2Dot`/`c2Mulvs`. Cause: `mulss` returns its *destination* operand when that's a NaN, and GCC picked the opposite operand order from LLVM. Notably, `_mm_mul_ss` intrinsics did **not** fix it — LLVM lowers them to a commutative `fmul` and re-commutes right back to identical machine code. Pinning the order required inline `asm!` (`mulss`/`addss` with an explicit `inout` destination), with portable `a * b` fallbacks under `cfg(not(target_arch = \"x86_64\"))`.\n\nWorth flagging: IEEE-754 leaves NaN result signs unspecified, so both versions were arguably \"correct\" — this only mattered because the bar is byte-identical. It is also invisible through `circle_collide` (the only header-declared function), which returns an `int` and never mismatched.\n\n## Faithfulness notes\n\nBugs preserved deliberately, not fixed: `c2CircletoCapsule` still divides by `c2Dot(n, n)` with no zero guard (degenerate capsules produce inf/NaN), and `c2Collided` still reinterprets `A` as a `c2Circle` regardless of `typeB`. Min/max use C's `a > b ? a : b` ternaries rather than `f32::max`/`min`, which disagree on NaN.\n\nCleanup: my `cbuild/` and `verify/` scratch dirs are removed; `c_src/` is untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":50561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c86d6a-f819-4259-98aa-2d66fbf769ee","uuid":"6278e3e0-61e3-4976-af77-666b0303ba37","timestamp":"2026-08-27T06:36:32.366Z"}
